# STRICT, AND FROM DAY ONE. Every check below is one whose finding is a DEFECT or an unarguable
# improvement. What is switched off is switched off with a reason beside it -- a disabled check with
# no reason is a check somebody re-enables next year and disables again.
#
# THIS TREE IS NEW, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE. A strict analysis over a grown tree finds
# thousands and is therefore introduced in stages; here there is nothing to stage. The baseline is 0
# because it can be. There is no "stage two": a stage without a date is a promise.
#
# NO FINDING COUNTS STAND BESIDE THE EXCEPTIONS, because there was nothing to count yet. Each
# exception below therefore rests NOT on a measurement but on the claim that its finding is taste.
# When one is put on a measurement, the number goes beside it (board:0005).
# `readability-redundant-member-init` is switched off ON A MEASUREMENT, which is what board:0005
# asks of an exception. It calls 88 initialisers in `meta/Declare.h` and `meta/TableDef.h`
# redundant; removing them does not compile, because they are DEFAULT MEMBER INITIALISERS and
# without them a designated aggregate must name every field:
# `KeyDef{.name = "PK", .fields = Date::kKey1, .clustered = true}` becomes
# `error: missing field 'sumIndexFields' initializer [-Wmissing-designated-field-initializers]`
# under `-Werror` (measured 2026-09-07). The check argues with another diagnostic, and the one that
# refuses to build wins.
#
# AND A COMMENT MAY NOT STAND INSIDE `Checks:`. It is a folded scalar, so `#` is text there and the
# reason silently became a check name -- the 88 findings did not move until it was lifted out here.

# `modernize-use-nodiscard` is switched off because AL DISCARDS. `[Ok := ] Xmlport.Export()` is the
# documentation's own shape: the return is bracketed, and a body that calls it as a statement is
# ordinary AL. Adding the attribute made generated code fail under `-Werror`
# (`apps/base/sales/customer/page/CustomerPicture.cpp:68`, measured 2026-09-07) -- the check is
# arguing with the language, not with us.
#
# `readability-convert-member-functions-to-static` is switched off because AN AL METHOD IS CALLED
# ON AN INSTANCE. `Blob.Export(Name)`, `Media.ImportStream(...)`, `Notification.Recall()` are how AL
# spells them, and a body that refuses until board:0030 brings a client touches no member YET -- the
# check reads "make it static" from a body that is a placeholder. Making it static would also break
# the registration shape: every subscriber and every test is registered through a MEMBER FUNCTION
# POINTER (`InvokeSubscriber<C, &C::M>`), which a static member cannot form.
#
# IT WAS ALREADY OFF, four times, in `NOLINT` regions -- `src/rt/Door.cpp`, `src/rt/RecordRef.cpp`,
# `include/type/Variant.h`, `include/runtime/RecordRef.h`. A reason repeated in four files is a
# reason that belongs here once, and moving it lowers the silent-places count rather than raising
# it (2026-09-08).
#
# `readability-redundant-casting` called `static_cast<T &>(value)` in `Materialised` redundant, and
# without it `T &` will not bind: `error: non-const lvalue reference to type 'int' cannot bind to a
# temporary` (measured 2026-09-07). A cast that makes the binding is not a cast that says nothing.

# `bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters` is SET TO THREE rather than switched off. AL's own
# signatures put two alike parameters side by side and this tree may not change them: `record-insert-boolean-boolean-method.md` is `Record.Insert(RunTrigger, InsertWithSystemId)`
# and `textbuilder-remove-integer-integer-method.md` is `Remove(StartIndex, Length)`. Name equality
# with AL is an architectural invariant here, so the two adjacent parameters are the specification.
#
# `modernize-avoid-c-arrays` refuses `Char(const char (&text)[N])`, which is the ONLY way a string
# literal binds while its length stays a compile-time constant -- `std::array` cannot take a literal.
# The parameter is how a one-character AL literal reaches `Char` at all.
#
# `misc-unconventional-assign-operator` wants `operator=` to return `Table&`; the door returns
# `Derived&`, which is CRTP working as intended and is what lets a generated table chain.
#
# `bugprone-branch-clone` reads `TextOf`'s `if constexpr` chain, where `Decimal` and the general
# `requires { value.ToInvariantString(); }` share a BODY and not a condition. The order decides
# which of a type's two renderings is used, so merging them would change the answer.

# `clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding` IS ON, WITH ITS THRESHOLD SET IN `test/lint.sh`. It found 57 padding bytes in `FieldDef` -- stored once per field -- and the
# reorder took it from 568 to 512 bytes and the library from 938.40 to 936.53 MB over 27 666 fields
# (measured 2026-09-07). What it names now is `Declared`, and that one is NEVER STORED: it is the
# parameter object `Declare()` takes, so its 48 bytes cost nothing at rest. Following it there means
# reordering the generator's emission too, because C++ ties a designated initialiser to the
# declaration order -- 101 lines of generator, a transpile and a full build, for zero bytes.
#
# `optin.performance.Padding:AllowedPad` is the threshold, and it travels the way the node budget
# travels -- as an `-analyzer-config` argument in `test/lint.sh`. Under `CheckOptions` it never
# arrives, because the analyser reads its own configuration and not clang-tidy's.
#
# THE OLD TEXT, kept because it says what the check is worth:: it found 57 padding bytes
# in `FieldDef`, which is stored once per field -- 568 bytes became 512 and the library lost 1.99 MB
# over 27 666 fields (measured 2026-09-07). It is set to 64 rather than switched off, because the
# one struct it still names is `Declared`, and that one is never stored: it is the parameter object
# `Declare()` takes, so its padding costs a register spill and nothing at rest. Its member order is
# also the order the GENERATOR emits designators in, which C++ ties together -- reordering it for a
# saving that does not exist cost 80 build errors.

HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(include|src)/.*\.h$'
FormatStyle: file
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  concurrency-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  modernize-*,

  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix,
  -readability-math-missing-parentheses,
  -readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -readability-redundant-member-init,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -readability-redundant-casting,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -misc-unconventional-assign-operator,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static
WarningsAsErrors: '*'

CheckOptions:
  # `misc-include-cleaner` maps `popen` and `pclose` to <stdio.h>, and
  # `modernize-deprecated-headers` forbids naming that header. The two checks contradict each other
  # and both are right in their own terms: these are POSIX functions and POSIX has no C++ header for
  # them. Ignoring the one header resolves it at the narrowest point available -- neither check is
  # switched off, and every other missing include is still a finding.
  # `bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters` is SET rather than switched off: AL's own signatures put
  # two alike parameters side by side -- `Record.Insert(RunTrigger, InsertWithSystemId)`,
  # `TextBuilder.Remove(StartIndex, Length)` -- and name equality with AL is an invariant here.
  # Three in a row is nobody's specification, so the check keeps that half of its reach.
  bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters.MinimumLength: '3'

  # `signal.h` is the same contradiction as `stdio.h` above, one header further: `sigaltstack`,
  # `stack_t` and `sigaction` are POSIX and have no C++ header, `<csignal>` carries only the four
  # names the standard names, and `modernize-deprecated-headers` forbids writing `signal.h`. The
  # runtime needs the POSIX three so a crash can print its frames -- on an ALTERNATE STACK, because
  # a stack overflow is the crash a handler on the overflowed stack cannot report (board:0616).
  misc-include-cleaner.IgnoreHeaders: 'stdio.h;signal.h'

  # `readability-identifier-length` belongs SET, not switched off. Its default asks for three
  # characters, which is wrong here: the tree carries AL vocabulary, and `i`, `n`, `no` are the
  # clearest names an index, a count and a `No.` will ever have. At one it still refuses the truly
  # nameless and stops arguing about loop counters.
  # `misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes` stays ON -- CLAUDE.md's own sentence is that a
  # public data member is an invariant nobody can hold. What it must not do is argue with AL. A
  # `TestPage` reaches its filters as `Page.FILTER.SETFILTER(...)`, a MEMBER access with no
  # parentheses -- which is why the documentation gives `TestFilter` a directory of its own under
  # `methods-auto/` rather than listing those methods on `TestPage`. Written as a method instead it
  # cost 82 errors over the 58 UT codeunits, because the rule that restores AL's missing
  # parentheses adds them to the link of a chain that is the CALL, and `FILTER` is not it.
  #
  # The narrowest lever available: a class whose data members are ALL public holds no mixed
  # encapsulation for the check to protect. One with a private member beside a public one still
  # does, and is still a finding.
  misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes.IgnoreClassesWithAllMemberVariablesBeingPublic: true

  readability-identifier-length.MinimumVariableNameLength: 1
  readability-identifier-length.MinimumParameterNameLength: 1
  readability-identifier-length.MinimumLoopCounterNameLength: 1

  # SHAPE RATHER THAN CORRECTNESS -- the only guard here that measures FORM. The default is 25 and
  # it stays. A generator emitter above it is one function that wants to be three.
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: 25

  # CLAUDE.md: every number carries its origin. What stays allowed are the numbers that CANNOT have
  # an origin, because they are the identities of arithmetic.
  readability-magic-numbers.IgnoredIntegerValues: '0;1;2;3;4;10;100'
  readability-magic-numbers.IgnoredFloatingPointValues: '0.0;1.0;100.0'

# WHY THESE FOUR ARE OFF, AND WHY NOTHING ELSE IS
#
# A check is off when its finding is NOT A DEFECT, and there are exactly two ways for that to be
# true: the finding is a matter of TASTE, or the DOMAIN already fixes the answer and the check is
# arguing with AL rather than with us. The first four below are taste. The last two are the second
# kind, and each carries its reason and its compensating guard rather than an opinion. Everything
# whose finding is a defect is ON and its counter reads zero.
#
# `modernize-use-trailing-return-type` wants `auto f() -> int`. This tree writes `int f()`, and so
#   does the rest of the world.
# `readability-uppercase-literal-suffix` wants `1.0F` over `1.0f`. LLVM house taste; it buys no
#   reader anything.
# `readability-math-missing-parentheses` parenthesises `a * b + c`. Precedence is not a defect, and
#   the parentheses hide the shape of an expression rather than showing it.
# `readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator` forbids `a ? b : c ? d : e`. Mapping an AL option
#   onto a C++ value is exactly that chain, and splitting it into `if` makes it longer, not clearer.
#
# `misc-no-recursion` reports every function in a recursive call chain. THE DOMAIN FIXES THIS ONE
#   TOO: recursive descent IS the shape of a parser, and this tree will grow one over AL expressions
#   that nest by construction. What the check is really about is UNBOUNDED depth, and that is
#   answered where it belongs -- every recursive reader here carries an explicit depth limit and
#   raises when it is crossed, rather than growing the stack until the process dies. Rewriting a
#   parser iteratively to satisfy a name would trade a checked bound for an explicit stack nobody
#   reads.
#
# `performance-enum-size` would size an enumeration by its largest enumerator. THE DOMAIN FIXES THIS
#   ONE: `methods-auto/option/option-data-type.md` says the Option type is "a zero-based enumerator
#   type ... You can convert option data types to integers", and an AL Integer is 32 bits. Every
#   option enumeration the generator emits is therefore `std::int32_t`, and an option's value round
#   trips through that enumeration -- narrowing it would truncate an ordinal outside the declared
#   members, which AL permits and this runtime keeps. The check would save three bytes in a name
#   table that never leaves `.rodata` and buy a silent truncation for it.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ON, EVEN THOUGH IT HURTS
#
# `misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes` -- CLAUDE.md's own sentence: a public data member
#   is an invariant nobody can hold. It does not reach generated Record classes, because `src/app/`
#   is not analysed at all.
# `readability-magic-numbers` -- CLAUDE.md's rule that every number carries its origin. It has
#   already paid for itself: chasing a bare `32` out of the Decimal divider exposed a silent lost
#   carry in the wide multiply.
# `bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters` -- `TableId`/`FieldNo`/`EntryNo` are all `int32`, and AL
#   swaps them silently. That is what the strong types in CLAUDE.md are for; this check is their
#   guard. It has twice been answered with better structure rather than an exception.
# `misc-include-cleaner` -- sharp on the standard library and often wrong beside it. It stays fully
#   on until a measurement on THIS tree shows otherwise; then the number goes in the line above and
#   `IgnoreHeaders` below it, in that order. An exception before the measurement would be a guess.
# `modernize-avoid-c-arrays` and `modernize-avoid-c-style-cast` -- free in a new tree.
